## Section 4 — Data Pipeline Issues

### Issue G — No price normalization before Kalman filter

**File:** `data_loader.py` — raw adj close prices used

The prices go from ~$10 to ~$200. When `sigma_X = std(diff(x1))` is computed, it is in **dollar** units (~$1-5/day). The H matrix encodes `x1[t]` which ranges over $10–$200. This means the Kalman gain and observation equations are numerically sensitive to the absolute price level. Normalize to base 1.0 (price / price[0]) before fitting.

### Issue H — Train/test split does not re-normalize to base 1.0

If you normalize the **formation period** to base 1.0 but then hand the **raw** out-of-sample prices to the filter, the initial state z0 will be wrong (it expects x1[0] ≈ 1.0 but gets x1[0] ≈ $50 or whatever the formation-end price was). The fix: normalize the FULL series to base 1.0 before splitting.

