## Section 7 — Known Good Pairs vs Problematic Pairs

Based on typical literature findings and pair characteristics:

| Pair | Formation Corr | Typical MR Strength | Notes |
|------|---------------|---------------------|-------|
| KO/PEP | ~0.80 | Strong | Same sector, oligopoly; best MR pair |
| EWA/EWC | ~0.92 | Strong | Near-identical commodity exposure |
| XOM/CVX | ~0.88 | Moderate | Good but broken during oil shocks |
| GS/CVX | ~0.50 | Weak | Cross-sector; MR only episodic |
| **AAP/IBM** | **~0.30–0.50** | **Very weak** | **Cross-sector; retail vs tech — not a valid pair** |
| NKE/AES | ~0.35 | Very weak | Cross-sector; problematic |
| MRK/VZ | ~0.40 | Weak | Cross-sector; healthcare vs telecom |

**AAP–IBM is not a cointegrated pair.** They are in completely different sectors (auto parts retail vs enterprise tech). The correlation is low and episodic. This pair should be **excluded or used only as a negative control** to test that the regime classifier correctly flat-lines it.

